1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,016
The Poltergeist: how do you fight something you can't see?

2
00:00:03,016 --> 00:00:03,905
You don't. You run.

3
00:00:04,125 --> 00:00:05,427
Here's how she plays.

4
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:10,643
Carolyn and Mr. Floppy are always in the game, hidden in the Item decks, and neither

5
00:00:10,643 --> 00:00:11,588
can start face up.

6
00:00:11,808 --> 00:00:16,457
Take ten of the Location's Items, set one aside for each deck, shuffle the rest with

7
00:00:16,457 --> 00:00:20,940
Carolyn and Mr. Floppy, deal them face down, then put a set-aside card face up on

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,493
each deck.

9
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,905
The Poltergeist has no health and can't be attacked, damaged or killed.

10
00:00:26,125 --> 00:00:28,821
To win, find Carolyn and reach an exit with her.

11
00:00:28,821 --> 00:00:32,077
When Carolyn joins you, remove all Minor Dark Power cards.

12
00:00:32,297 --> 00:00:36,013
Carolyn can't be killed, discarded or put in your backpack, though she can be

13
00:00:36,013 --> 00:00:37,268
shuffled back into a deck.

14
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,068
Mr. Floppy can't be used until her Dark Power is revealed.

15
00:00:41,068 --> 00:00:43,626
After that, you can remove him to ignore 'Carolyn?

16
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:44,393
Where are you?'

17
00:00:44,613 --> 00:00:48,165
If her Epic Dark Power, Forgetting Something?, comes out, you need Mr.

18
00:00:48,165 --> 00:00:49,840
Floppy as well as Carolyn to win.

19
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:54,704
A few tips. Searching matters more than saving Victims here, so head for a Search

20
00:00:54,704 --> 00:00:55,701
space straight away.

21
00:00:55,921 --> 00:00:59,740
Selena is a great pick: an early Ultimate and extra search dice.

22
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:04,141
Carry Guard for her Unstoppable Evil attacks, and don't waste Time on weapons.

23
00:01:04,361 --> 00:01:08,610
She's tougher than average: Final Girls win about fifty-seven percent of logged

24
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:09,524
games. Good luck.

